    "content": "Arsenal and Manchester City are set to contest the 2026 FA Community Shield this afternoon, but the traditional curtain-raiser of the English football season will not take place at the usual venue. The match will be held at Principality Stadium in Cardiff, Wales, the first time in two decades that this fixture has been played in the Welsh capital.\n\nSources at the Football Association confirmed that Wembley Stadium is unavailable for the match because it is hosting large-scale events today that were arranged long in advance. These commitments left the London venue unable to accommodate the football match, necessitating the move to Cardiff. The Principality Stadium, known primarily for rugby, has previously hosted football matches, including during the 2012 Olympic Games.\n\nThis year's Community Shield brings together the Premier League champions, Manchester City, and the FA Cup winners, Arsenal. The two clubs have a fierce rivalry, and this match offers an early chance for silverware and momentum ahead of the new season. For Arsenal, it is an opportunity to build on their recent domestic cup triumphs, while Manchester City aim to continue their dominance under their current manager.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom follow English football fervently, this venue change is notable. It allows fans in Wales and the surrounding regions to see top-tier football locally, perhaps making it easier for some to attend. Additionally, it serves as a reminder of how major football events can adapt to logistical challenges, ensuring that the show goes on for supporters around the world, including those tuning in from Somalia and other countries.\n\nThe match is scheduled to kick off at the usual early afternoon time, with fans in Cardiff set to witness a high-stakes encounter. Both teams have named strong squads, and the neutral venue may level the playing field, though Manchester City will still be considered favorites given their recent head-to-head record against Arsenal.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/08/16/sababta-arsenal-iyo-manchester-city-looga-saaray-wembley/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sababta-arsenal-iyo-manchester-city-looga-saaray-wembley",
