    "summary": "The Somali government has announced that national carrier Somali Airlines will restart direct flights in September 2026, ending a 35-year hiatus. Officials say required preparations have been completed.",
    "content": "In a renewed push to revive the country's national airline, Somalia's federal government has announced that Somali Airlines will resume direct flights in September 2026. The announcement was made by Ahmed Moallin, the director of the Somali Civil Aviation Authority, who stated that all necessary groundwork has been completed and that the airline is expected to begin operations shortly.\n\nSomali Airlines, once a symbol of national pride, ceased operations in 1991 amid the onset of civil conflict. For over three decades, Somalia has lacked a fully functioning national carrier, leaving the country's air travel largely dependent on foreign airlines and private operators. The revival of Somali Airlines is seen as a milestone in the country's ongoing reconstruction efforts.\n\nThe government has previously floated plans to relaunch the airline, but this is the most concrete timeline yet. According to Moallin, the approval process and technical preparations have been finalized, paving the way for the airline's return to the skies. The initial focus will be on direct routes, though specific destinations have not been disclosed.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, which numbers in the millions and maintains strong ties to their homeland, the resumption of a national carrier holds particular significance. It promises more direct connectivity, potentially more competitive fares, and a tangible symbol of Somalia's recovery. Many in the diaspora have long called for reliable and affordable air links between Somali cities and international hubs.\n\nWhile challenges remain, including fleet acquisition and operational sustainability, the announcement signals progress in rebuilding key national institutions. The resumption of Somali Airlines would not only boost economic ties but also facilitate family visits and business travel for Somalis at home and abroad. Observers will be watching closely to see if the September timeline is met.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/16/dawladda-soomaaliya-oo-sheegtay-in-diyaaradda-somali-airlines-ay-bisha-soo-socata-billaabayso-duulimaadyada/",
